# Strapi Integration Rules

## Fetch Layer
- All Strapi API calls go through `frontend/lib/strapi.ts` — never write raw fetch calls to Strapi in components or pages
- Base URL always from `process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_STRAPI_URL` — never hardcoded
- If token-based server access is needed, keep it server-side only (never `NEXT_PUBLIC_`)

## Query Patterns
- Always use `populate` explicitly — never assume nested relations come back automatically
- Always use `filters`, `pagination`, and `sort` params server-side — don't filter/sort client-side
- Prefer specific field selection with `fields` param over fetching entire documents

## Type Safety
- Every Strapi response gets a typed interface in `frontend/lib/types.ts`
- Validate response shape at the fetch boundary — don't spread unknown API responses directly into components
- Strapi v5 responses are flattened in this project; normalize to frontend-safe shapes before returning from `strapi.ts`

## Error Handling
- All fetch functions in `strapi.ts` use try/catch with typed errors
- Return `null` or a typed error state on failure — never let fetch errors bubble uncaught to the UI
- Log errors server-side; surface a safe fallback to the client

## Caching
- Articles/resources: choose revalidate intentionally (document the chosen interval)
- Use `cache: 'no-store'` only for preview/draft endpoints